% in 2026Q1, then fell 4% in 2026Q2. That is the first decline in three years.\n- Shipments trail orders by about two quarters. A Q2 drop therefore suggests orders were already weak in late 2025 or early 2026. The weakness is likely to carry into H2 2026 and possibly early 2027.\n\n**Voltaris's revenue run-rate**\n- Voltaris's last four quarters were 905, 960, 980 and 890 (C$M), which sums to about C$3.74B.\n- Q2 2026 fell about 9% from Q1. Annualised, that is about C$3.56B.\n\n**What guidance requires**\n- C$4.2B is about 12% above the trailing four quarters. It is about 18% above the Q2 run-rate.\n- That growth would have to come in an industry that is shrinking. Voltaris would need to gain share substantially, or prices or mix would have to improve a lot.\n\n**Estimate**\n- If Voltaris holds its share and the industry is flat to slightly down, 2027 revenue would be about C$3.5–3.8B.\n- Reaching C$4.2B would need a sharp industry recovery in 2027 plus share gains. That looks unlikely on this evidence, so there is a shortfall of roughly 10–15%.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The CEA maker table, which would show Voltaris's share and whether it is gaining or losing, was not retrievable.\n- Shipments are a lagging indicator, and Voltaris's own backlog (the other node's question) could offset this view.","ttft_ms":1414,"type":"result","duration_ms":44582,"uuid":"43f0b87c-a0b7-4c75-9e18-9e80964f0754","ttft_stream_ms":1069,"time_to_request_ms":139,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":19,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":22,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":18,"query_setup":2,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":8,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_r